
                                                🐧 What is Linux?

Linux is a "free and open-source", "Unix-like operating system" built around the "Linux Kernel".

It was created by "Linus Torvalds" and the first Linux kernel was released on "17 September 1991".

Unlike a complete operating system, the Linux kernel is only the core component. A full Linux operating system is
created by combining the Linux kernel with software such as GNU utilities, package managers, desktop environments,
and other system tools.


                                                 ✨ Key Features

- 🆓 Free and Open Source
- 🔒 Secure and Reliable
- ⚡ High Performance
- 🌍 Multi-user and Multitasking
- 📦 Supports Thousands of Applications
- 💻 Runs on Servers, Desktops, Embedded Devices, and Supercomputers


